;; source_line: 710816
(#$ist #$CoreCycLMt (#$comment #$completeByNature "An instance of #$CompletenessGroundsPredicate (q.v.) that is used to state, about a collection or predicate whose extent is inferentiallly complete (see #$InferenceCompletenessPredicate), that the completeness derives mainly from the nature of the collection or predicate itself (or the nature of the items in its extent), rather than from any conventional stipulation. For example, (#$completelyDecidableCollection #$Integer) holds, and so does (#$completeByNature #$Integer). In contrast, #$completeByNature does <i>not</i> hold of the completely-asserted collection #$DayOfWeekType. Cf. #$completeByConvention."))
;; source_line: 712018
